# Dashboards

Lovelace runs in **storage mode** (`lovelace: mode: storage` in `configuration.yaml`). Dashboards are stored in `.storage/lovelace*`; those four files are explicitly allowed by `.gitignore` so the UI travels with the config repo.

## Design principles

- **Automations + templates first**: minimize manual touch. Template sensors, groups, labels, Jinja2 templates do the dynamic work.
- **Responsive**: started at section width 3, dropped to 2 to fit wall pads and small screens.
- **Single unified surface**: left sidebar hidden, everything lives in one Lovelace view.
- **HomeKit-inspired**: design follows Apple HomeKit conventions, fitting the iPhone-heavy household.

## Key features

- **Dynamic sections**: Home / Climate / Energy / System and so on — purpose-driven splits.
- **Interactive cards**: media, lights, HVAC are directly actionable.
- **Custom visuals**: combination of custom cards + themes.
- **Live updates**: weather forecast, traffic, system status all refresh in real time.

